[38;5;231m⏺[39m Going with the inline bar (A). The rest of the questions are here in the terminal.

  The next one affects how the CSS gets written. The guidelines say page CSS has to use the semantic tokens ([38;5;153m--space-4[39m,
  [38;5;153m--border-focus[39m, [38;5;153m--text-secondary[39m and so on) from a "shared token sheet". I can't find that sheet anywhere in this
  repo. [38;5;153mactivity.css[39m is the only stylesheet, and it uses raw hex and px values, which the reviewers flag.

  So the question is where the token values come from:

  - [1mLink the existing sheet:[0m if the token sheet is served from a known path (for example by ops' nginx), I link it from
    [38;5;153mactivity.html[39m and write the new CSS with [38;5;153mvar(--token)[39m only. This keeps the diff smallest and matches the guidelines
    exactly. I just need the path from you.
  - [1mAdd the tokens to this page:[0m I add a [38;5;153m:root[39m block that defines only the tokens the filter bar uses, with values
    copied from the table in guideline 01. Reviewers get token-only CSS. The cost is a second copy of those values that
    could drift from the real sheet, and it could be removed later once the shared sheet is linked.
  - [1mRaw values:[0m I write the new CSS the same way as the existing file. It's quick, but every one of those values would
    draw a review comment, so I'd rather not.

  I recommend the first option if the sheet exists somewhere, and the second if it doesn't. Separately, I won't change
  the raw values already in [38;5;153mactivity.css[39m unless you say that's in scope. That would be its own [38;5;153mfix:[39m commit.

  Where should the token values come from? If you choose the first option, include the path.

